{"id":"n3-048","title":"～てごらん (〜te goran)","jlptLevel":3,"shortExplanation":"Suggest or invite someone to try doing something; 'Why don't you try...'.","longExplanation":"The ～てごらん grammar point is used to gently suggest or invite someone to try doing something. It is softer and more casual than ～てみて, and is used among friends or family.","formation":"Verb-て form + ごらん","examples":[{"jp":"そのゲームをやってごらん。","romaji":"Sono geemu o yatte goran.","en":"Why don't you try playing that game?","words":[{"surface":"その","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ゲーム","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"やっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"やる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ごらん","vocabId":"1270760","reading":"ごらん"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5]},{"jp":"彼に話してごらん。","romaji":"Kare ni hanashite goran.","en":"Try talking to him.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"話し","vocabId":"1562350","reading":"はなす","baseForm":"話す"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ごらん","vocabId":"1270760","reading":"ごらん"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"新しいレシピを作ってごらん。","romaji":"Atarashii reshipi o tsukutte goran.","en":"Why don't you try making a new recipe?","words":[{"surface":"新しい","vocabId":"1361490","reading":"あたらしい"},{"surface":"レシピ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"作っ","vocabId":"1597890","reading":"つくる","baseForm":"作る"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ごらん","vocabId":"1270760","reading":"ごらん"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5]},{"jp":"そのドレスを着てごらん。","romaji":"Sono doresu o kite goran.","en":"Try putting on that dress.","words":[{"surface":"その","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ドレス","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"着","vocabId":"1597470","reading":"ちゃく","baseForm":"着る"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ごらん","vocabId":"1270760","reading":"ごらん"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":